%% rabbitmq consumer_timeout: disabled.
%%
%% The default (30 min) and any finite ceiling misfire on this system: a
%% slow-but-alive handler (a live broadcast or a long vod transcode exceeds
%% any limit) gets its delivery redelivered mid-run, spawning a duplicate
%% transcode that corrupts output files. Dead consumers don't need the
%% timeout — their connection drops and unacked messages requeue on their
%% own — so the timeout only ever produces false positives here.
[{rabbit, [{consumer_timeout, undefined}]}].
